## Notes on the fix

- **Desktop mode now resolves the panel**: `config/apps.js` declares `component: 'solopreneur'`; `Desktop.vue` renders panels from `ALL_COMPONENTS`, so registering `SolopreneurView` there is the single missing link. `Desktop.vue` needs no edit.
- **No more dockview teardown on section clicks**: `goModule()` mutates `state.module` and only pushes the route in single/mobile mode (`$storex.ui.isDesktopMode === false`). In a panel, clicking *Account / Projects / Wallet…* stays inside the panel.
- **Route remains the deep-link source** for `/solopreneur/:module?`; unknown modules still fall back to `summary` via `setModule()`.
- **Layout now follows the real width**: `@container` + `@5xl`/`@6xl`/`@4xl`/`@3xl` (Tailwind v4 container queries, already used in `DesktopView.vue`) replace the window-based `lg:`/`xl:`/`2xl:` classes, so a wide panel renders the sidebar rail and side-by-side cards like the full-screen mockup.

