I'll inspect the current state of the view, the Tailwind setup, and how panels size their content in desktop mode.Let me read the desktop host and app registration to see how the panel wraps the view.Let me check how desktop panels mount their component (wrapper element, sizing), plus the global CSS height chain.Let me verify the Tailwind/CSS pipeline and how other dockview panel components root their templates (height chain).## Diagnosis

The regression comes from the container‑query rewrite in `SolopreneurView` + `SolopreneurSidebar` + `SolopreneurSummary`:

- The shell relies on `@container` + `@5xl:*` variants to switch `flex-col` → `flex-row` **and** `w-full` → `w-[276px]` for the rail. When the container variant on the width does not win over the base `w-full` (while the direction change does apply, or when the panel/route width never satisfies the variant), the `aside` keeps `w-full` while the row layout is active. With `shrink-0`, the rail then consumes the whole row and the content column (`flex-1 min-w-0`) collapses to **0 px** → exactly "only the left bar is shown".
- `@container` also injects `contain: layout style inline-size` on the root, which turns the root into the containing block for the `position: fixed` modals/toasts and makes the whole screen depend on one fragile mechanism.

## Fix

Make the responsive shell **deterministic and host‑agnostic**: measure the width the view is actually given (`ResizeObserver`) and drive the layout with explicit, mutually exclusive classes. All `@container` / `@5xl` / `@6xl` usages in the solopreneur components are removed; card grids become intrinsic (`auto-fit`) so they need no breakpoints at all.

### Changes Summary

| # | File | Change |
|---|------|--------|
| 1 | `useSolopreneur.js` | Add measured `viewport` state (`width`, `isWide`, `isXl`) + `setViewportWidth()`. |
| 2 | `SolopreneurView.vue` | Measure root width with `ResizeObserver`, pass `wide` to the rail, drive `flex-row`/`flex-col` explicitly; drop `@container`. |
| 3 | `SolopreneurSidebar.vue` | `wide` prop; width/border/padding/nav direction via ternaries instead of `@5xl:` variants. |
| 4 | `SolopreneurSummary.vue` | Intrinsic `auto-fit` grids (no breakpoints); calendar column only when `isXl`. |

