## Notes

- **Why the rail no longer eats the row:** `aside` gets exactly one width class (`w-[276px]` **or** `w-full`) and the root gets exactly one direction (`flex-row` **or** `flex-col`) — both derived from the same `state.viewport.isWide`, so they can never disagree.
- **Why it works in both hosts:** `ResizeObserver` on the view root measures the *actual* available width — the window on `/solopreneur`, the panel in desktop mode. No media queries, no container queries, no `contain` side effects on the fixed modals/toasts.
- **Thresholds:** `≥1024px` → rail beside content; `≥1280px` → calendar side column. Everything else (card pairs, glance tiles, project tiles) uses intrinsic `auto-fit` tracks, so it adapts between those tiers without extra breakpoints.
- **Mobile unchanged:** below 1024px the root is `flex-col`, the rail is a full-width horizontal nav, and the content column keeps `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`.

